      "source": "user",
      "user_confirmed": true,
      "value": [
        "On each rebalance day, the last session of each calendar month that has a next session, after the daily close, compute for every eligible stock the daily return r_t = Close_t / Close_(t-1) - 1 for each of the trailing 252 sessions, on the published adjusted closes",
        "A stock is ranked only when it has 253 consecutive closes on the official NSE sessions ending on the rebalance day, which gives 252 consecutive daily returns; a stock missing any session in that window is not ranked on that rebalance day",
        "Volatility is the sample standard deviation with ddof 1 of those 252 returns, not annualised",
        "Rank the ranked stocks from lowest to highest volatility; ties are broken by the platform's hash of symbol and date",
        "Hold the 30 stocks with the lowest volatility; a held stock that is still among the 30 is kept, not sold and bought again",
        "Buy orders for stocks that newly enter the 30 fill at the next session's open"
      ]
    },
